# Cpp code guidelines
- use camelCase for variable names and UpperCase for class or struct names
- prefer bmin containers/strings over STL (`bmin::DynArray`, `bmin::String`, `bmin::Map`) — see `bmin-containers.mdc`
- prefer using std::unique_ptr / bmin::UniquePtr or std::optional instead of raw pointers
- all cpp functions must be in a cpp file and not declared inline.
- every cpp file must be explicitly defined in the source file.
- all classes must exist within a namespace, if the namespace is the top level use the "program" namespace.
- prefer declaring variables with auto instead of the type, like: "auto a = int{1}".
- use structs for any groups of data or classes that have no methods.
- prefer const references if passing by reference.
- prefer using LOG macro from "sdl2w/Logger.h" instead of iostream or printf
- mark override when a method is overridden

## Class-local helpers (prefer members over anonymous namespaces)

When a helper is only used by one class, put it on that class — not in an anonymous namespace in the `.cpp`.

- **Prefer** private (or private `static`) member functions and `static constexpr` members on the class.
- **Do not** stash class-owned helpers or constants in `namespace { ... }` just to hide them from the linker.
- **OK** to keep free functions / anonymous-namespace helpers when they are shared across translation units' peers, true file-local utilities with no owning class, or small observer/adapter types that follow an existing pattern (e.g. button observers).

```cpp
// ❌ BAD — helper belongs to LayerWorld but lives in an anonymous namespace
namespace {
bool canPlayerIssueCombatMove(const state::State& state) { ... }
void enqueueMapMove(state::StateManager& stateManager, int dx, int dy) { ... }
}

// ✅ GOOD — private static members on the class
class LayerWorld : public Layer {
  static bool canPlayerIssueCombatMove(const state::State& state);
  static void enqueueMapMove(state::StateManager& stateManager, int dx, int dy);
};
```

For UI layout/sprite constants specifically, also see `cpp-ui.mdc`.